{"results":[{"url":"https://abcnews4.com/news/local/rhode-island-democratic-party-leader-apologizes-for-tweet-about-grahams-covid-diagnosis","final_url":"https://abcnews4.com/news/local/rhode-island-democratic-party-leader-apologizes-for-tweet-about-grahams-covid-diagnosis","title":"RI Democratic Party strategist apologizes for tweet about Graham's COVID diagnosis","description":"COLUMBIA, S. C. (WCIV) &mdash; A top official in the Rhode Island Democratic Party has apologized for a tweet regarding South Carolina Senator Lindsey Graham. Kate Coyne-McCoy, who is currently an executive consultant for The Ocean State's democrats, took to Twitter Tuesday morning after previously tweeting about Graham's COVID-19 diagnosis. In a now-deleted tweet screen-grabbed by Fox News, she wrote, \"It&rsquo;s wrong to hope he dies from Covid right? Asking for a friend. #COVIDISNOTOVER #LINDSEYGRAHAM. \"","language":"en","text":"# RI Democratic Party strategist apologizes for tweet about Graham's COVID diagnosis\n\n---\n\nby MATT DILLANE | WCIV Staff\n\nTue, August 3, 2021 at 9:04 AM\n\nUpdated Tue, August 3, 2021 at 10:53 AM\n\nA top official in the Rhode Island Democratic Party has apologized for a tweet regarding South Carolina Senator Lindsey Graham. (AP Photo/Manuel Balce Ceneta)\n\nCOLUMBIA, S.C. (WCIV) — A top official in the Rhode Island Democratic Party has apologized for a tweet regarding South Carolina Senator Lindsey Graham.\n\nKate Coyne-McCoy, who is currently an executive consultant for The Ocean State's democrats, took to Twitter Tuesday morning after previously tweeting about Graham's COVID-19 diagnosis.\n\nView post on X\n\nIn a now-deleted tweet screen-grabbed by Fox News, she wrote, \"It’s wrong to hope he dies from Covid right? Asking for a friend. #COVIDISNOTOVER #LINDSEYGRAHAM.\"\n\nOn Monday, the Republican lawmaker became the first senator to share news of experiencinga breakthrough infection after being vaccinated.\n\nGraham said he“started having flu-like symptoms Saturday night” when heattended a gathering on Sen. Joe Manchin’s houseboat. He went to see a doctor on Monday morning.\n\n***Related Content:Graham is first vaccinated senator to test positive for COVID-19***\n\nView post on X\n\nThe lawmaker said he would now be quarantining for 10 days.","author":"MATT DILLANE | WCIV Staff","published_date":"2021-08-03T13:04:53.000Z","latency_ms":1184.1683920010837,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}